@ 37.2.5.2 - Proto-Crow-Hidatsa to Hidatsa
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan I”. International Journal of American Linguistics 16(2):61 – 66; Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan II” International Journal of American Linguistics 16(3):113 – 121; Wolff, Hans (1950), “Comparative Siouan III”. International Journal of American Linguistics 16(4):168 – 178; and cedh audmanh’s changes above, which assisted me in deciphering the vintage phonetic transcription scheme NB: Does not include developments in unstressed non-nasal vowels.
	n > r
	ʔ > ∅ / C_
	kr > kVrV / #_
	r > ∅ / {C,V}k_{C,V}
	mn > w / {C,V}_{C,V}
	sn > t͡sVrV
	km > hp
	sk > t͡suk / _”u
	sk kx > t͡sk hk / _”V
	sk > ht͡s / ”V_
	∅ > V / x_k